：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:59:  - 第一步：识别所有竖直灰色路径和所有水平色带。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:60:  - 第二步：对于每条灰色路径，记录它从上到下依次穿过的色带颜色序列。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:61:  - 第三步：该路径的输出颜色由它穿过的第一条（最上方的）色带的颜色决定。将整条路径（包括穿过色带的交叉点）重新着色为该颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:62:  - 第四步：色带本身保持不变。如果路径的新颜色与其穿过的某条色带颜色相同，则在该交叉点处路径颜色优先显示。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:63:- `Key insight`：解题者需要先识别出\"色带\"和\"路径\"是两种不同的结构元素，然后发现路径颜色由其穿过的第一条色带决定——而不是由最后一条、最多的一条或路径本身的位置决定。色带的排列顺序本身是一种编码系统。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:64:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:65:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:66:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:67:- `description`：将网格中的多个小图案按照它们与边框连接线的拓扑关系重新排列到指定的输出槽位中。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:68:- `Input structure`：背景色网格的四条边上各有若干个单像素的彩色锚点（颜色各不相同）。从每个锚点出发，有一条同色的单像素宽线段向网格内部延伸（水平或竖直方向），线段末端连接着一个灰色的小矩形区域（约 3×3 到 5×5）。每个灰色矩形内部包含一个由非灰色、非背景色像素构成的独特小图案。网格中央有一个由灰色边框围成的大矩形输出区域，该区域内部被灰色线分割成若干个与小矩形等大的槽位。每个槽位的边缘有一个单像素彩色标记，颜色与某个边框锚点颜色对应。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:69:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:70:  - 第一步：识别边框上的每个彩色锚点，沿其连接线找到对应的灰色小矩形，提取其中的小图案。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:71:  - 第二步：在中央输出区域中，找到带有相同颜色标记的槽位。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:72:  - 第三步：将提取的小图案放入对应颜色标记的槽位中。图案在槽位中居中放置，保持原始朝向。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:73:  - 第四步：移除所有连接线和边框锚点，仅保留中央输出区域及其中填好的图案。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:74:- `Key insight`：解题者需要建立\"边框锚点颜色 → 连接线 → 源图案\"和\"槽位颜色标记 → 目标位置\"两条映射链，然后通过颜色匹配将两条链关联起来。颜色在这里不是装饰属性，而是路由地址。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:75:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:76:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:77:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:78:- `description`：根据每个对象被网格线切割后产生的碎片数目，决定该对象在输出中的存留或删除。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:79:- `Input structure`：背景色网格上有一组均匀分布的细虚线网格线（由间隔排列的灰色像素构成，水平和竖直各若干条），将网格划分成若干等大的格子。网格上还有若干个不同颜色的 4-连通实心对象，这些对象跨越多个格子，被虚线网格线切割。在网格的一个角落有一个小的\"图例区\"——一个由灰色边框围成的小方格，内部显示一个数字状的像素图案，表示阈值数 T（T 的值为 2 或 3，用像素点阵的方式画出）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:80:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:81:  - 第一步：识别虚线网格线将每个对象切割成的连通碎片数量（沿网格线将对象像素擦除后，统计剩余像素的 4-连通分量数）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:82:  - 第二步：读取角落图例中的阈值数 T。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:83:  - 第三步：如果一个对象被切割成的碎片数量严格大于 T，则在输出中保留该对象（恢复被网格线擦除的像素，即完整显示该对象）。如果碎片数量小于或等于 T，则将该对象完全删除（替换为背景色）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:84:  - 第四步：虚线网格线在输出中全部移除。角落图例也移除。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:85:- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现虚线网格线的\"切割\"作用——它们不是装饰，而是将对象拆分成碎片的工具；然后需要归纳出\"碎片数与阈值比较\"这一筛选规则。两层推理都非显然：第一层需要理解网格线的功能含义，第二层需要从样例中归纳出阈值比较的方向（大于而非小于）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md:86:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:1:你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:3:每个参考题描述包含：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:4:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:5:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:6:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"7acdf6d3\" lines=\"25-42\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:11:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:12:Move the source-color pixels into the unique outline interior whose size matches the source count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:13:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:14:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:15:- The grid has a dominant background and exactly two foreground colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:16:- One foreground color forms 8-connected outline objects with row-wise interior cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:17:- The other foreground color supplies a set of source pixels away from the chosen outline.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:18:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:19:- For each possible outline color, compute each 8-connected outline object's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:20:  row-span interior: background pixels strictly between the leftmost and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:21:  rightmost outline pixels on each occupied row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:22:- Select the unique outline interior whose cell count equals the total\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:23:  number of pixels of the other foreground color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:24:- Erase the source pixels and paint that matched interior with the source color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:25:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:26:- The colors are roles, not fixed IDs: the source color is identified by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:27:  counting, and the destination is the outline with a matching interior area.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:28:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:29:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:30:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:31:<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e4941b18\" lines=\"8-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:32:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:33:Move red into teal's top marker position, then move teal to the bottom outside corner of the grey rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:34:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:35:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:36:- The dominant background surrounds one filled rectangular non-background block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:37:- There is exactly one red marker and one teal marker, both in the row immediately above the rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:38:- Both markers are horizontally aligned over columns inside the rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:39:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:40:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:41:- Clear the original red marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:42:- Recolor the original teal marker cell red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:43:- Place the teal marker beside the rectangle's bottom row, on the side indicated by the horizontal direction from red to teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:44:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:45:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:46:- The red-to-teal horizontal order chooses the rectangle side where teal exits at the bottom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:47:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:48:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:49:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:50:<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d6e50e54\" lines=\"8-25\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:51:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:52:Move each maroon marker toward the blue rectangle and recolor the rectangle red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:53:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:54:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:55:A background canvas contains one solid blue rectangular object and several isolated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:56:maroon marker pixels. Each marker is horizontally or vertically aligned with the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:57:rectangle and lies outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:58:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:59:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:60:Start with a background canvas, repaint the blue rectangle red, and move each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:61:maroon marker straight toward the rectangle along its row or column. Exactly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:62:marker is strictly closer to the rectangle than all others and enters the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:63:rectangle boundary; every other marker lands in the adjacent exterior cell just\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:64:outside its aligned side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:65:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:66:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:67:The single entering marker is the unique global nearest marker to the rectangle,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:68:not the nearest marker on each of the four sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:69:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:70:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:71:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:72:<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"35ab12c3\" lines=\"73-88\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:73:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:74:Complete outlined shapes and carry attached shadow pixels along their edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:75:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:76:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:77:- bg = background. Each active color marks vertices of an 8-direction aligned outline.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:78:- A start vertex can have adjacent non-bg, different-colored shadow pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:79:- Other colored pixels may be distractors unless they lie on valid drawable edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:80:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:81:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:82:- For each color, order its pixels by polar angle around their centroid to form a cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:83:- Draw only horizontal, vertical, or 45-degree edges whose interiors are clear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:84:- From the chosen start vertex, copy adjacent shadow offsets along each drawable edge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:85:  when the parallel path is in bounds and clear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:86:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:87:Key insight: The main outline is reconstructed first, then the start vertex's neighbor offsets define parallel shadow strokes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:88:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:89:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:90:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:91:<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"291dc1e1\" lines=\"7-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:92:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:93:Reorder and stack rectangles by proximity to two colored edge lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:94:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:95:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:96:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:97:- Two edge lines (h + v) meet at a corner marked by a unique color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:98:- \"Blue\" line is color 1 if present, else the longer line; other is \"red.\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:99:- Solid rectangles in the interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:100:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:101:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:102:- Sort rectangles by (distance to blue edge, distance to red edge).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:103:- If the blue edge is vertical, rotate each rectangle 90° CCW.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:104:- Stack top-to-bottom, centered horizontally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:105:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:106:Key insight: Edge-line colors encode a coordinate system; proximity to each axis determines stacking order and rotation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:107:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:108:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:109:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:110:<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"edcc2ff0\" lines=\"47-63\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:111:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:112:Keep only the lower-panel colors named by the top markers and expand each marker into an object-count bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:113:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:114:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:115:A black instruction strip sits above a non-black rectangular scene panel.  The strip contains one-cell markers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:116:in the first column, and each marker color is a candidate object color in the lower panel.  The lower panel has\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:117:a unique dominant background color and scattered 4-connected foreground objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:118:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:119:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:120:In the lower panel, preserve objects whose colors appear as top markers and recolor every other foreground\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:121:object to the panel background.  In the instruction strip, replace each marker by a horizontal run from column 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:122:whose length is the number of 4-connected lower-panel objects of that marker color; erase markers with count 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:123:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:124:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:125:The top strip is a color filter plus a compact count summary: marker colors select which lower-panel objects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:126:survive, and their bars report the number of surviving objects by color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:127:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:128:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:129:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:130:<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"80a900e0\" lines=\"69-82\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:131:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:132:Extend diagonal rays outward from outer-border segments adjacent to diamond shapes on a checkerboard.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:133:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:134:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:135:- Checkerboard bg (two most common colors).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:136:- Hollow diamond outlines (8-pixel) in a non-bg color (inner border).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:137:- Short diagonal line segments in another non-bg color adjacent to each diamond edge (outer border).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:138:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:139:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:140:- For each outer-border segment, determine the outward direction (perpendicular to the segment, away from the diamond).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:141:- From each endpoint of the segment, cast a diagonal ray outward, painting over bg pixels with the segment's color until hitting a non-bg pixel or the grid edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:142:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:143:Key insight: Rays emit only from the two endpoints of each outer-border segment, not every pixel, and travel diagonally away from the diamond.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:144:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:145:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:146:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:147:<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f1bcbc2c\" lines=\"40-55\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:148:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:149:Paint the top-connected middle channel between two orange path components teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:150:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:151:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:152:- The background is black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:153:- One foreground color forms exactly two 4-connected one-pixel-wide path components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:154:- Optional non-background control pixels may sit in the channel between the two paths.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:155:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:156:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:157:- Dilate each path component by one cell in the 8-neighborhood and intersect the two dilations; this gives the one-cell-wide middle channel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:158:- A control pixel in that channel is a blocker only when its 4-neighbors touch fewer than both path components; otherwise it is part of the channel and is repainted.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:159:- After removing blockers, paint the channel component connected to the top edge teal and keep all other pixels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:160:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:161:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:162:- The desired pixels are not found by region filling; they are the geometric overlap of the two paths' one-cell halos, with weakly attached control pixels splitting the channel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:163:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:164:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:165:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:166:<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"52364a65\" lines=\"10-24\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:167:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:168:Erase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:169:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:170:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:171:- A grid has one dominant background color and several monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:172:- Each foreground object spans at least two columns in its bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:173:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:174:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:175:- Find each same-color 4-connected foreground object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:176:- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:177:- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:178:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:179:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:180:- The deletion is measured from each object's local left edge, not from the grid edge or from a shared global column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:181:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:182:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:183:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:184:<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2de01db2\" lines=\"28-41\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:185:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:186:Invert each row's native foreground color against the black background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:187:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:188:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:189:- A black-background grid whose rows each have one native foreground color plus optional distractor colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:190:- The native row color is the most frequent non-bg color in that row; if tied, its run starts leftmost among tied colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:191:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:192:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:193:- For each row independently, turn pixels of the native row color into bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:194:- Turn every other pixel in that row, including bg and distractor colors, into the native row color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:195:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:196:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:197:- Distractor colors are not preserved objects; they mark cells that participate in the binary complement of the row's native color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:198:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:199:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:200:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:201:<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"da6e95e5\" lines=\"70-81\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:202:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:203:Extract the central object from the marker cluster whose markers have the same color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:204:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:205:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:206:The grid has a dominant background and several clusters; each cluster has four\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:207:same-color corner marker objects around one central monochromatic object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:208:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:209:Find every central object enclosed by four aligned corner markers of one color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:210:then choose the unique one whose object color equals the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:211:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:212:The answer is not the largest or most frequent object; it is the center of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:213:self-colored cluster, cropped to that object's bounding box with background kept.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:214:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:215:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:216:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:217:<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"98c475bf\" lines=\"62-76\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:218:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:219:Erase the complete interior glyph and expand each endpoint marker pair into its color's full glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:220:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:221:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:222:- The grid is 20x20 with background inside two same-color full-height vertical frame bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:223:- Inside the frame there is one complete color glyph and one or more other colors appearing only as two endpoint markers in the same row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:224:- Marker endpoints are always in the first and last interior columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:225:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:226:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:227:- Keep the vertical frame unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:228:- Erase any complete interior glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:229:- For each endpoint marker pair, use that marker color's learned glyph template and anchor its horizontal bar on the marker row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:230:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:231:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:232:- Color identifies which glyph shape to draw; the two endpoint pixels are not copied objects, they are anchors for reconstructing that color's full symbol.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:233:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:234:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:235:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:236:<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2ba387bc\" lines=\"6-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:237:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:238:Sort scattered 4×4 squares into two columns by type: frames left, solids right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:239:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:240:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:241:- bg = most common color. Multiple 4×4 objects on bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:242:- Frames: colored 1px border, bg-filled 2×2 interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:243:- Solids: entirely filled with one non-bg color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:244:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:245:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:246:- Classify each 4×4 object as frame or solid by its interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:247:- Sort each group top-to-bottom by input row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:248:- Stack frames in left column (cols 0–3), solids in right (cols 4–7).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:249:- Output is 8 wide; height = 4 × max(#frames, #solids), bg-padded.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:250:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:251:Key insight: Frame vs solid is determined solely by whether the 2×2 interior matches bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:252:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:253:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:254:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:255:<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"337b420f\" lines=\"41-55\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:256:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:257:Keep the larger sprite from each separated panel and overlay those sprites into one 5x5 canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:258:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:259:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:260:- The input is a 5x17 grid: three 5x5 panels separated by one-cell black columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:261:- Each panel has the same background color and exactly one foreground color split into two 4-connected components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:262:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:263:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:264:- In each panel, discard the smaller foreground component and keep the unique largest component as the sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:265:- Process panels left to right, placing each sprite at its panel coordinates on a 5x5 background canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:266:- If a sprite would cover an already placed sprite, slide it by the unique nearest in-bounds offset that avoids overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:267:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:268:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:269:- The extra same-colored component in each panel is a distractor; the final answer is the non-overlapping overlay of the three largest components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:270:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:271:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:272:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:273:<reference_puzzle index=\"15\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"18447a8d\" lines=\"33-48\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:274:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:275:Move each right-side colored shape into the left slot whose template color is its exact complement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:276:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:277:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:278:- The grid has two equal-width slots separated by one background column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:279:- Non-background rows form horizontal bands separated by all-background rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:280:- Each band has a shared template color in the left slot and one colored source shape in the right slot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:281:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:282:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:283:- For each band, define its destination shape as the cells in the left slot not occupied by the template color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:284:- Normalize every right-side source shape to right-slot coordinates and match it to the unique equal destination shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:285:- Clear the original right-side source pixels and paint the matched left-slot complement with the source color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:286:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:287:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:288:The right-side objects are not placed by row order; each one completes the unique left template whose missing cells have the same shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:289:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:290:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:291:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:292:<reference_puzzle index=\"16\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"bc93ec48\" lines=\"48-63\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:293:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:294:Copy each foreground object anchored in a true grid corner clockwise into the next corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:295:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:296:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:297:- The dominant color is the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:298:- Foreground objects are monochromatic 4-connected components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:299:- Relevant objects are exactly those whose bounding box touches two adjacent borders at one grid corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:300:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:301:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:302:- Start from the input unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:303:- For each corner object, copy its pixel mask and color to the next corner clockwise: top-left to top-right, top-right to bottom-right, bottom-right to bottom-left, and bottom-left to top-left.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:304:- Preserve each object's orientation by aligning its bounding box to the destination corner; stamps may overwrite existing pixels at the destination, but source pixels are not cleared.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:305:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:306:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:307:- Interior and side-only objects are distractors; only components actually anchored to a corner participate in the clockwise perimeter copy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:308:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:309:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:310:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:311:<reference_puzzle index=\"17\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"89565ca0\" lines=\"120-136\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:312:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:313:Convert each colored partitioned frame into a horizontal bar whose length is its number of enclosed regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:314:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:315:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:316:- Black background with several axis-aligned colored line drawings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:317:- The line drawings are damaged by scattered pixels of one non-background noise color and by overlaps with other drawings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:318:- Each real drawing is a rectangular partitioned frame enclosing one or more background regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:319:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:320:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:321:- For each non-background color, reconstruct its horizontal and vertical wall segments from dense row/column evidence.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:322:- Count the 4-connected background regions fully enclosed by those reconstructed walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:323:- The color with no enclosed region is the noise/pad color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:324:- Sort drawing colors by enclosed-region count; equal counts are ordered by which reconstructed frame covers the other.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:325:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:326:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:327:- The scattered color is not an object; it only pads the histogram, while each true object's room count is stable after rectilinear wall reconstruction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:328:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:329:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:330:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:331:<reference_puzzle index=\"18\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"c920a713\" lines=\"87-102\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:332:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:333:Untangle overlapping colored rectangular frames into concentric square frames ordered by their visible crossings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:334:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:335:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:336:- The background contains several one-cell-thick axis-aligned rectangular frames, one color per frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:337:- Frames overlap, and the visible color at an overlap records a directed crossing from the hidden frame to the visible frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:338:- Each foreground color still has visible pixels on the perimeter of its full rectangular bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:339:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:340:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:341:- Infer each color's full rectangular frame from the bounding box of its visible pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:342:- Add a directed edge A -> B when B is visible at a crossing of A and B's frame perimeters.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:343:- Find the unique path that visits every frame color once, then render those colors as one-pixel-thick concentric square frames from outside to inside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:344:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:345:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:346:- The output is not a crop of the input; the crossing graph gives a single frame order, and that order is redrawn as nested rings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:347:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:348:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:349:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:350:<reference_puzzle index=\"19\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"78332cb0\" lines=\"10-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:351:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:352:Reorder 5×5 blocks into a connected strip by matching edge foreground pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:353:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:354:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:355:- bg = background; sep = divider color (full row/column lines).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:356:- Several 5×5 sprite blocks in a grid, separated by sep lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:357:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:358:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:359:- Two blocks \"connect\" when their facing edges share foreground pixels at the same offset (e.g., A's right edge ∩ B's left edge).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:360:- Chain all blocks in the orientation (horizontal or vertical) that admits a complete sequence.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:361:- Output is a 1×N strip of blocks in chain order, separated by sep lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:362:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:363:Key insight: Edge-contact overlap determines both block ordering and output orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:364:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:365:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:366:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:367:<reference_puzzle index=\"20\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"faa9f03d\" lines=\"36-52\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:368:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:369:Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by replacing singleton markers, filling short orthogonal gaps, and redirecting yellow-marked arms to the edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:370:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:371:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:372:- A rectangular grid with a dominant background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:373:- Line colors form one-cell-thick horizontal/vertical stroke fragments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:374:- Marker colors are exactly those whose 4-connected components are all singleton pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:375:- Red singleton markers are missing line cells; yellow singleton markers are directional controls next to a line endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:376:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:377:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:378:- Assign every marker to the nearest visible line color in row/column line-of-sight, preferring an endpoint supported along that same axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:379:- For each line color, fill the gap between consecutive facing endpoints in a row or column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:380:- A yellow control erases the old straight arm on the far side of its endpoint and paints the same color from that endpoint through the control pixel to the grid edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:381:- At crossings, yellow-control rays win; otherwise an original-vs-filled crossing uses the more fragmented pre-repair line color, while pure filled crossings use the lower color id.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:382:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:383:Key insight: The singleton markers identify which sparse stroke fragments belong together; after they are colored, the intended lines are the axis-aligned gaps between facing endpoints, with yellow controls flipping one arm to the marked side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:384:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:385:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:386:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:387:你的任务：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:388:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:389:创新方式包括但不限于：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:390:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:391:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:392:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:393:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:394:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:395:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:396:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:397:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:398:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:399:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:400:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:401:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:402:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:403:请一次性生成5个`<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:404:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:405:注意事项：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:406:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:407:2. 关于\"计算\"的边界：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:408:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:409:   - **禁止使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算（取模） / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算都是禁止使用的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:410:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id和颜色亮度是禁止使用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:411:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:412:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:413:6. 新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:414:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:415:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:416:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\"结构层数\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\"找到缺口在哪一侧\"、\"数出像素个数\"、\"识别哪个对象最大\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:417:   - ✗ 伪两层：\"找到缺口方向\"→\"把东西推到对面\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:418:   - ✓ 真两层：\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\"→\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:419:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:420:   如果你发现自己写出的题只是\"对每个对象，根据它的某个属性做某变换\"的单步规则，请引入一个需要主动推理的前置步骤。**用堆叠 tie-break 规则或复杂数学公式来\"加难度\"是劣解；用多一层需要归纳的结构嵌套来\"加难度\"才是好解**。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:421:10. 在符合ARC题目和提示词要求的基础上，鼓励尝试创新规则为多层结构的题目，不局限于两层，可以创新三层或四层结构的题目，但不可为了多结构层数违背要求。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:422:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:423:生成后对生成的题执行以下四项审查（审查内容不需要保存到文件）：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:424:1. 原创性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:425:  新题不可与上述参考题相同或类似，不可只是替换颜色、方向、对象类型等表层要素。判断标准：新题的核心推理路径应与任何一道参考题不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:426:2. 确定性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:427:  规则完全确定，同一输入只能产生唯一输出，每一步操作都有明确定义。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:428:3. 可实现性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:429:  所有必要细节都已给出——对象如何生成、如何识别、如何变换、边界情况如何处理，读完描述后可以直接写代码。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:430:4. ARC 合规性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:431:  网格尺寸合理（≤30×30），使用颜色不超过 10 种，规则复杂度适中，人类能从 3-5 个样例中发现规律。没有使用上述注意事项第二条禁止使用的复杂计算。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md:432:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
